From 3648686ceda60c11481593b308da5923342d1b47 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 17:25:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Check device recipes' signatures, and let the system
 remove them

A recipe's packages now install only with valid signatures: the media
must carry the repository database's signature, and pacman checks it and
every package against a keyring that holds the recipe's key and nothing
else, made only when that key is the one the recipe names. A recipe whose
key does not match is left out entirely.

The installed system gets omarchy-recipe. It says what the recipe is and
that it is not part of Omarchy, lists what came from it and which of
Omarchy's packages it replaces, and fetches the repository's signed
description daily. A pacman hook passes on the maintainer's notice once
the repository is retired, and omarchy-recipe remove takes it out of
pacman.conf, drops its key, reinstalls Omarchy's own build of every
package Omarchy has, and with --purge removes the ones only it had.

The recipe installs from the media or the install fails. The first-boot
fallback is gone: the stick is made to be complete, and a machine without
its recipe may have no Wi-Fi to fetch it with (the Surface Pro 11's board
file comes from the recipe). A failure now stops the install with pacman's
output in the log instead of a system that looks installed and is not.

What makes the stick complete: the image's offline mirror has only what
every install needs, and a recipe's packages depend on more of Omarchy's
and Arch Linux ARM's own packages (the Surface's sensors, iptsd,
iio-sensor-proxy and their libraries). The USB creator now puts those
under recipe/official/ with their upstream signatures, and the installer
installs them first with pacman -U and LocalFileSigLevel = Required, so
the system keyring (Omarchy's and Arch's keys) checks each one. The
recipe's own key still signs nothing but the recipe's own packages.

Fixed on the way: the loop copying the recipe's files reused the variable
holding the repository's name, so /etc/omarchy/recipe/repo said
"info.json.sig", pacman -Slq found no packages, and nothing was installed.
The copy is its own function now, with a test on what it writes.

Tested: test/all passes, with a new test of omarchy-recipe against
stubbed pacman, keyring tests with a real ed25519 key, and tests of the
saved recipe files and the official packages' listing and pacman.conf.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
